WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.354 --> 00:00:09.186
The Agents page is your team. Every agent has a card with its role, model, current work and how it performs against the others in its role.

2
00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:13.091
Open Agents in the sidebar, then choose Hire agent.

3
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:19.913
Pick the role and the seniority. The runtime and the effort come from the role, and you can change them here.

4
00:00:20.612 --> 00:00:28.057
Under Where may this agent work, tick the projects it is allowed on. Give it a name, and Hire. It appears on the page at once.

5
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.947
Pause stops an agent from taking new work; a running shift still finishes. Resume puts it back to work.

6
00:00:35.646 --> 00:00:43.497
Change model switches an agent to another model or effort. It applies from its next shift, and the agent keeps its name and history.

7
00:00:44.209 --> 00:00:52.337
Recommendations are rule-based suggestions with their evidence. Here two builders have been idle for ten days while the queue is empty.

8
00:00:53.037 --> 00:00:57.752
Apply one with its button: Fire retires Cleo, and the card says what was done.

9
00:00:58.451 --> 00:01:06.792
Dismiss the other if you disagree. It will not be suggested again for thirty days. With several open, Dismiss all clears them in one go.

10
00:01:07.495 --> 00:01:14.428
The Project filter shows only the agents allowed on one project, and the Department filter does the same for a department.

11
00:01:15.132 --> 00:01:25.116
An agent can also move to another workstation. Choose Move on its card, pick the workstation, and choose Move. Its name, history and track record go with it.

12
00:01:25.815 --> 00:01:31.191
That is the Agents page. Hire the team you need, and keep it tuned with the recommendations.
